WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.517 --> 00:00:05.982
This is the Ship tab. A ship is a hull, four parts, a sea crystal and a crew.

2
00:00:12.158 --> 00:00:16.166
Each slot takes the best part you own, or one you pick yourself.

3
00:00:16.166 --> 00:00:20.458
Type your Sailing Mastery in here. It counts toward speed.

4
00:00:21.184 --> 00:00:23.945
And every number on the card moves with it.

5
00:00:23.945 --> 00:00:28.504
Now the crew. Eighteen sailors with four growths each is a lot of typing.

6
00:00:28.504 --> 00:00:33.662
And you cannot guess them: a sailor's real rolls are what make the speed match the game.

7
00:00:33.662 --> 00:00:37.122
So it reads them off your screenshots instead.

8
00:00:37.802 --> 00:00:43.363
Screenshot the Manage Sailors window in game, one sailor per shot, and drop them in.

9
00:00:43.363 --> 00:00:47.094
It reads them here in your browser. Nothing is uploaded.

10
00:00:47.094 --> 00:00:51.151
It works through them and gives you a table, not a roster.

11
00:00:52.416 --> 00:00:58.329
Check it against the game first — a misread level should cost you a glance, not your crew.

12
00:01:02.977 --> 00:01:05.493
Then take the ones that are right.

13
00:01:05.493 --> 00:01:09.636
Save a whole fit-out under a name, and switch between them.

14
00:01:10.048 --> 00:01:13.737
And copy the lot as a link, if someone asks what you sail.

15
00:01:13.737 --> 00:01:19.522
That is your ship. Every number on it is either yours, or read off your own screen.
